// Storage rules for Cuboid Studio's full-resolution encode photos.
//
// ⚠️ THIS FILE IS A BLOCK TO MERGE, NOT A RULESET TO PASTE WHOLESALE.
//
// The bucket belongs to the shared `adaptivememeticarchitect-2776f` Firebase
// project, and archthesis already stores every meme image in it under
// `memes/`. Publishing this file as the complete ruleset would delete
// whatever protects those images and could break archthesis.
//
// To publish: open the CURRENT rules (Firebase console → Storage → Rules),
// keep everything already there, and paste ONLY the match block below inside
// the existing `match /b/{bucket}/o { … }`.
//
// Storage rules are also deployed separately from Firestore rules: archthesis's
// deploy workflow ships firestore.rules and never touches these, so nothing
// republishes (or overwrites) them automatically.
//
// Layout: compositionPhotos/{ownerId}/{fileName}
// A composition document keeps a 240px thumbnail inline and points at the
// original here by path. Only the authenticated owner may read or write their
// own photographs.

// ---- paste from here ----
    match /compositionPhotos/{ownerId}/{fileName} {
      allow read, write: if request.auth != null
                         && request.auth.uid == ownerId;
    }
// ---- to here ----


// For reference only — what the finished ruleset looks like if the bucket had
// nothing else in it. Do NOT use this if the console already shows rules.
//
// rules_version = '2';
